# Environment Variable Configuration Template
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Instructions:
# 1. Copy this file to '.env' in this folder: cp .env.example .env
# 2. Fill in only what you need. Everything is optional for public GitHub repos.
# 3. NEVER commit your actual '.env' file or any real secrets to Git.
# Tokens are read from the environment only, never from command-line arguments.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- GitHub (optional) ---
# Raises the API limit from 60 to 5,000 requests/hour. A fine-grained token with
# no extra permissions (public repositories, read-only) is enough.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=your_github_token_here

# --- Gemini via Google ADK (optional, only for --ai) ---
# Create a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey. Usage may incur costs or hit quotas.
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-flash-latest

# --- Sentry (optional, for --source sentry) ---
# Auth token with read access (scopes: event:read, project:read).
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=your_sentry_token_here
# SENTRY_ORG=your-org-slug
# SENTRY_PROJECT=your-project-slug
# SENTRY_URL=https://sentry.io

# --- GlitchTip (optional, for --source glitchtip) ---
# Create a token under Profile > Auth Tokens with event:read.
# GLITCHTIP_AUTH_TOKEN=your_glitchtip_token_here
# GLITCHTIP_ORG=your-org-slug
# GLITCHTIP_PROJECT=your-project-slug
# GLITCHTIP_URL=https://app.glitchtip.com
